# Portal day sync roadmap (A → B)

Victor chose **all of it**, starting with **A**. Capacity-chain **phases / occupants standing stay** — this roadmap consumes them; it does not replace them.

## Option A — DONE (Staff = Overview client visibility)

- Shared module: `working_ui/portal/portal_client_day_visibility.js` (`PortalClientDayVisibility`)
- Overview (`admin-sessions-hub.js`) and Staff Today (`staff-dashboard-today.js`) use the **same** `clientAllowedOnDate` / weekday / Fadi-off / gone-from / fallback starts / finish-booking first_session index.
- Staff still applies audience projection at the end: worker scope + aquatic merge + covers. Do **not** reintroduce a second start-date map on Staff only.

## Hygiene (same root cause, before / during B)

- **Timesheet** is another parallel reader. Do not invent shifts by projecting a dated cover onto later same-weekdays.
- Gate: standing projection onto an ISO only if **Autumn Instructor Timetable** names that worker that day (`PORTAL_AUTUMN_STAFF_HOURS`). Exact dated rows + cover injects still apply.
- Example fixed: John Hub Multi **Sun 6** cover must not paint **Sun 13 / 20** (Timetable has no John those days; Hub standing = Berta / Emmanuel / Godsway).

## Option B1 — LANDED (shared day-board core + Feedback 20:30 board policy)

Module: `working_ui/portal/portal_resolve_day_board.js` (`PortalResolveDayBoard`)

```
resolveDayBoard(iso, audience) → { seats, meta }
  1. standing = capacity chain rows (STAFF_DASHBOARD_SOURCE)
  2. dated overlays (session_date === iso) in those rows
  3. schedule_overrides / unavailability — still hydrated by Overview/Staff callers
  4. exceptions via PortalRosterCanonical.applyCapacityChainDayExceptions (on chain resolve)
  5. PortalClientDayVisibility filter
```

| Wired | How |
|-------|-----|
| **Timesheet** | `workerOnAutumnTimetableIso` + `standingSnapIsoForDow` delegated to module |
| **Overview** | `hubLatestStandingIsoForDow` prefers module snap |
| **Staff** | `portalAutumnStandingSnapIsoForWeekday` prefers module stamp |
| **Feedback 20:30** | `applyFeedback2030BoardPolicy` — roster wins over MADRE; cover twin remaps (Raul→Victor / Sandra→Javi) retired; OV owns covers |

Audience paint (aquatic merge, staff columns, pay bands) stays outside the core.

